proof.text:
*Factorization through a finite stage.* $\Lambda$ is finite, hence Noetherian (a finite ring is a Noetherian module over itself; Mathlib `isNoetherian_of_finite`, Mathlib/RingTheory/Noetherian/Basic.lean:123), and this is the only place where the hypothesis 'Noetherian $\Lambda$' of Stacks enters the proof. $X$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated and $F$ is constructible, so by [lem-weil-pbc-constructible-finitely-presented] the map $\varphi:F	o
u_*\underline M_Y=\operatorname{colim}_i
u_{i,*}\underline M_{Y_i}$ factors as $F\xrightarrow{\varphi_i}
u_{i,*}\underline M_{Y_i}\xrightarrow{\kappa_i}
u_*\underline M_Y$ for some $i$, with $\kappa_i$ the colimit injection. For every geometric point $ ar x$ over $x$, $(\kappa_i)_{ ar x}\circ(\varphi_i)_{ ar x}=\varphi_{ ar x}$ is injective (previous steps), so $(\varphi_i)_{ ar x}$ is injective. Set $f_x=
u_i:Y_x=Y_i	o X$, finite, $M_x=M$, a finite $\Lambda$-module, and $\varphi_x=\varphi_i:F	o f_{x,*}\underline{M_x}$. (Stacks: 'By Lemma 09Z4 the map $\mathcal F	o f_*\underline E$ factors through $f_{i,*}\underline E$ for some $i$'. Stacks' further remark that $Y_i	o Z$ is finite etale over a nonempty open of $Z$ belongs to the 'Moreover' clause, which this node does not state.)
